✘ Test "R-SYN-11: a space sweep counts a followed job it re-queues ahead of the next parked job, which is parked in the sweep's turn when the room left does not hold it (F-22)" with 2 test cases failed after 3.667 seconds with 2 issues.
↳ /// A space sweep counts the bytes of a followed job it re-queues ahead of the jobs it judges after it, as it does for
↳ /// any re-queued job. The setup of `spaceSweepRequeuesAFollowedJobItsNewLaneFits` (C, 5 MB, wanted by A's user waiter
↳ /// and B's prefetch waiter; no room for user work, 6 MB for prefetch work, 4 MB pending reclaim; A moved to a 16-byte
↳ /// content while the bounded follow owes C's visit) plus D (7 MB, a prefetch waiter) parked `awaitingSpace` behind C.
↳ /// After the reclaim prefetch work has 10 MB: C fits its prefetch lane and is re-queued; counted ahead, it leaves D
↳ /// 5 MB, so D is parked `insufficientSpace` in the sweep's own turn and its fail-fast answers D's waiter with D's 7 MB
↳ /// against that room. A re-queue that did not count C ahead re-queued D too, over-admitting the room until the gate
↳ /// parked it again (the close-out cycle-7 requirements lens, PROBE-C7R-GAIN-AHEAD, mutant `gainNoAhead`).
↳ ///
↳ /// Hang guard (S3-R4): under TSan in the whole Sync bundle it took 33.8 to 34.9 s beside a second TSan
↳ /// process at a load of 1.9 to 18.6 (58 % of 60 s) and 22.2 s alone at a load of 9 to 11 (Stage 3
↳ /// close-out cycle 8), over half its 60 s, so the guard is `.minutes(3)`, as for the tests of the same setup in
↳ /// `EngineFollowTests`.
✘ Test "R-SYN-11: one space sweep turn parks at most parksPerPump jobs and leaves the rest to its follow-up sweep (C2)" failed after 3.680 seconds with 2 issues.
↳ /// One turn of a space sweep parks at most `parksPerPump` jobs and leaves the rest to its follow-up sweep (C2). The
↳ /// park of a job whose follow lowered its lane during the sweep (`sweepSpaceParked`, PROBE-C5-LANEDROP, close-out
↳ /// cycle 6) goes through the same bound, so this count pins both; the turn's length is measured by the release
↳ /// benchmarks of parking a 10,000-member group and of a reclaim during an owed follow. The setup is
↳ /// `reclaimedSweepReachesEveryWaitingMember`'s: more members than one turn parks wait `awaitingSpace` for `x`'s
↳ /// 300 bytes on a volume with no other room above the reserve; the store reaps `x` and the purge path's `.reclaimed`
↳ /// sweep runs with its follow-ups held (`holdSpaceSweepFollowUps()`): its one turn re-queues the first member into
↳ /// the 300 bytes and parks exactly `parksPerPump` of the others `insufficientSpace` (nothing is left to reclaim).
↳ ///
↳ /// Hang guard (S3-R4): under TSan in the whole Sync bundle it took 41.7 to 43.1 s beside a second TSan process at a
↳ /// load of 20 to 35 (72 % of 60 s) and 18.4 s alone at a load of 13 to 18 (Stage 3 close-out cycle 7; the cycle-6
↳ /// verifier measured 32.2 to 32.8 s paired at a load of 17 to 34), over half its 60 s, so the guard is
↳ /// `.minutes(3)`.
